<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elizabeth Stuart, Queen of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1596">1596</a>–<a href="/years/1662">1662</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Winter Queen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elizabeth Stuart was the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i">James VI and I</a> and the wife of Frederick V, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a>, whom she married in 1613. Her husband's acceptance of the Bohemian crown made her queen for a single winter in 1619–1620, hence her name, the Winter Queen, and the couple spent their exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>. Through her daughter Sophia, electress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, the British throne passed to the house of Hanover in 1714.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elizabeth-stuart-queen-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Elizabeth Stuart, Queen of Bohemia" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Michiel Jansz. van Mierevelt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Workshop_of_Michiel_Jansz._van_Miereveldt_Elizabeth_Stuart_Queen_of_Bohemia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
